To find the difference between $325_{8}$ and $237_{8}$ in base $8$, we can perform the subtraction directly in base $8$. First, we align the numbers:
\[
\begin{array}{c@{}c@{}c}
 & 3 & 2 & 5_{8} \\
- & 2 & 3 & 7_{8} \\
\cline{2-4}
\end{array}
\]
We start from the rightmost digit. Since $5_{8}$ is less than $7_{8}$, we need to borrow from the next column. After borrowing, we have $15_{8} - 7_{8} = 6_{8}$. Moving to the next column, we have $1_{8}$ (after borrowing) and $2_{8}$, and again, we need to borrow, so we have $12_{8} - 3_{8} = 7_{8}$. Finally, in the leftmost column, after borrowing, we have $2_{8} - 2_{8} = 0_{8}$. Therefore, the difference is $67_{8}$.</think> <think>think>67</think> </think> <think>think>67</think> </think>

